    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.notify\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nHello echasnovski. I have come across a problem where I want to enable transparency for mini.notify but am not able to. Even though I set the background to NONE for MiniNotifyNormal, MiniNotifyTitle and MiniNotifyBorder, transparency is not enabled for mini.notify. I am unable to figure out what to do and taught I could get some assistance by raising a bug request.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nv0.10.0-dev-3117+g4e5c633ed\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nJust use mini.notify and try enabling transparency.\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nWanted transparency.\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nTransparency is not coming.",
