        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> ```lua\r\n> vim.cmd.colorscheme(\"tokyonight\")\r\n> vim.cmd(\"au ColorScheme * highlight MiniNotifyNormal guibg=NONE\")\r\n> vim.cmd(\"au ColorScheme * highlight MiniNotifyTitle guibg=NONE\")\r\n> vim.cmd(\"au ColorScheme * highlight MiniNotifyBorder guibg=NONE\")\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nThis is the main issue: you first enable color scheme and *after* that create autocommands that should react to color scheme change. Putting `vim.cmd.colorscheme(\"tokyonight\")` after autocommands creation *should* solve the issue.\r\n\r\nIn reality, there needs to be one extra adjustment: use `config.window.winblend = 0` in 'mini.notify'. This is because with `winblend > 0` doesn't work nicely with \"transparent\" floating windows (see neovim/neovim#10685).",
