        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> > ```lua\r\n> > vim.cmd.colorscheme(\"tokyonight\")\r\n> > vim.cmd(\"au ColorScheme * highlight MiniNotifyNormal guibg=NONE\")\r\n> > vim.cmd(\"au ColorScheme * highlight MiniNotifyTitle guibg=NONE\")\r\n> > vim.cmd(\"au ColorScheme * highlight MiniNotifyBorder guibg=NONE\")\r\n> > ```\r\n> \r\n> This is the main issue: you first enable color scheme and _after_ that create autocommands that should react to color scheme change. Putting `vim.cmd.colorscheme(\"tokyonight\")` after autocommands creation _should_ solve the issue.\r\n> \r\n> In reality, there needs to be one extra adjustment: use `config.window.winblend = 0` in 'mini.notify'. This is because with `winblend > 0` doesn't work nicely with \"transparent\" floating windows (see [neovim/neovim#10685](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/10685)).\r\n\r\nIt works thank you for helping me out.",
